## Review Checklist

### Component Architecture

- [ ] Components are properly typed with TypeScript interfaces
- [ ] Components follow single-responsibility principle
- [ ] No manual `React.memo` / `useCallback` / `useMemo` added "just in case": the React
      Compiler (on in Expo SDK 54+ templates) memoizes; manual memoization needs a measured
      reason in a comment (SUGGESTION to remove otherwise)
- [ ] React 19: `ref` passed as a normal prop, no new `forwardRef` (SUGGESTION)
- [ ] Components stay compiler-friendly: no mutating props/state, no reading refs during render (WARNING)

### State Management

{% if variables.state_library != 'None' %}
- [ ] {{ variables.state_library }} state contains ONLY UI state (BLOCKER if violated)
{% else %}
- [ ] No server/database data copied into component state or context (BLOCKER if violated)
{% endif %}
- [ ] React Query is used for all data fetching (BLOCKER if violated)
- [ ] Drizzle queries are in `src/db/queries/` (BLOCKER if violated)
{% if variables.state_library == 'Zustand' %}
- [ ] Zustand stores have a `reset()` method for testing
{% elif variables.state_library == 'Redux Toolkit' %}
- [ ] Slices have a `reset` reducer and typed selectors; components use `useAppSelector`
{% elif variables.state_library == 'MobX' %}
- [ ] MobX stores use `makeAutoObservable` and have `reset()`; readers are wrapped in `observer`
{% elif variables.state_library == 'Jotai' %}
- [ ] Jotai: one atom per value, derived atoms instead of duplicated state
{% endif %}

### TypeScript

- [ ] No `any` type usage (WARNING)
- [ ] No unsafe `as` type casts (WARNING)
- [ ] Props interfaces are exported for reuse

### Performance

- [ ] `FlashList` for lists with 20+ items (BLOCKER if ScrollView+map)
- [ ] No FlashList v1-only props (`estimatedItemSize`, `MasonryFlashList`, `inverted`) — removed/deprecated in v2 (WARNING)
- [ ] No unstable work in list `renderItem` that the profiler shows as slow (WARNING when measured)
- [ ] `expo-image` instead of `Image` from react-native (SUGGESTION)

### Platform-Specific

- [ ] `Platform.OS` checks where iOS/Android differ
- [ ] Tokens, refresh tokens and secrets in `expo-secure-store`, never AsyncStorage, MMKV or a persisted store (BLOCKER)
- [ ] `SafeAreaView` or `useSafeAreaInsets` for notch handling
- [ ] `KeyboardAvoidingView` with correct `behavior` per platform

### i18n

- [ ] All user-facing strings use `t('key')` (WARNING if hardcoded)
- [ ] Translation keys follow dot notation convention
- [ ] Any new key added to `src/i18n/locales/en.json` (the source catalog) — the
      i18n catalog-parity test will fail if other shipped locales drift (WARNING)
- [ ] Locales are NOT added/removed by hand — the supported set is fixed by the
      `languages` build option and must stay identical to the landing site (BLOCKER if changed ad hoc)

